208
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,900
So Boxing Day, as you said, is usually a Commonwealth thing.

209
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:55,080
In the United States, you don't really have it, right?

210
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:55,600
We do not.

211
00:10:56,080 --> 00:11:02,080
My family, I don't know why, but my family sometimes celebrates that we have friends who come over and we have a nice Boxing Day meal.

212
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:18,400
But I've been told that the tradition in Commonwealth countries is to watch sporting events, local sporting events, and to go shopping for all these sales and bargains and exchange all those ugly, hideous, annoying or bad gifts that you received at Christmas.

213
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,400
Right.

214
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,180
So it's usually like the after Christmas sales.

215
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:22,140
Exactly.

216
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:27,500
So if you have any special Boxing Day traditions, I'd be very curious to hear them.

217
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:31,160
Again, not a holiday related to the sport boxing.

218
